rewritten.\n2009 | \n2010 |         Parameters\n2011 |         ==========\n2012 | \n2013 |         args : Expr\n2014 |             A *rule*, or *pattern* and *rule*.\n2015 |             - *pattern* is a type or an iterable of types.\n2016 |             - *rule* can be any object.\n2017 | \n2018 |         deep : bool, optional\n2019 |             If ``True``, subexpressions are recursively transformed. Default is\n2020 |             ``True``.\n2021 | \n2022 |         Examples\n2023 |         ========\n2024 | \n2025 |         If *pattern* is unspecified, all possible expressions are transformed.\n2026 | \n2027 |         >>> from sympy import cos, sin, exp, I\n2028 |         >>> from sympy.abc import x\n2029 |         >>> expr = cos(x) + I*sin(x)\n2030 |         >>> expr.rewrite(exp)\n2031 |         exp(I*x)\n2032 | \n2033 |         Pattern can be a type or an iterable of types.\n2034 | \n2035 |         >>> expr.rewrite(sin, exp)\n2036 |         exp(I*x)/2 + cos(x) - exp(-I*x)/2\n2037 |         >>> expr.rewrite([cos,], exp)\n2038 |         exp(I*x)/2 + I*sin(x) + exp(-I*x)/2\n2039 |         >>> expr.rewrite([cos, sin], exp)\n2040 |         exp(I*x)\n2041 | \n2042 |         Rewriting behavior can be implemented by defining ``_eval_rewrite()``\n2043 |         method.\n2044 | \n2045 |         >>> from sympy import Expr, sqrt, pi\n2046 |         >>> class MySin(Expr):\n2047 |         ...     def _eval_rewrite(self, rule, args, **hints):\n2048 |         ...         x, = args\n2049 |         ...         if rule == cos:\n2050 |         ...             return cos(pi/2 - x, evaluate=False)\n2051 |         ...         if rule == sqrt:\n2052 |         ...             return sqrt(1 - cos(x)**2)\n2053 |         >>> MySin(MySin(x)).rewrite(cos)\n2054 |         cos(-cos(-x + pi/2) + pi/2)\n2055 |         >>> MySin(x).rewrite(sqrt)\n2056 |         sqrt(1 - cos(x)**2)\n2057 | \n2058 |         Defining ``_eval_rewrite_as_[...]()`` method is supported for backwards\n2059 |         compatibility reason. This may be removed in the future and using it is\n2060 |         discouraged.\n2061 | \n2062 |         >>> class MySin(Expr):\n2063 |         ...     def _eval_rewrite_as_cos(self, *args, **hints):\n2064 |         ...         x, = args\n2065 |         ...         return cos(pi/2 - x, evaluate=False)\n2066 |         >>> MySin(x).rewrite(cos)\n2067 |         cos(-x + pi/2)\n2068 | \n2069 |         \"\"\"\n2070 |         if not args:\n2071 |             return self\n2072 | \n2073 |         hints.update(deep=deep)\n2074 | \n2075 |         pattern = args[:-1]\n2076 |         rule = args[-1]\n2077 | \n2078 |         # support old design by _eval_rewrite_as_[...] method\n2079 |         if isinstance(rule, str):\n2080 |             method = \"_eval_rewrite_as_%s\" % rule\n2081 |         elif hasattr(rule, \"__name__\"):\n2082 |             # rule is class or function\n2083 |             clsname = rule.__name__\n2084 |             method = \"_eval_rewrite_as_%s\" % clsname\n2085 |         else:\n2086 |             # rule is instance\n2087 |             clsname = rule.__class__.__name__\n2088 |             method = \"_eval_rewrite_as_%s\" % clsname\n2089 | \n2090 |         if pattern:\n2091 |             if iterable(pattern[0]):\n2092 |                 pattern = pattern[0]\n2093 |             pattern = tuple(p for p in pattern if self.has(p))\n2094 |             if not pattern:\n2095 |                 return self\n2096 |         # hereafter, empty pattern is interpreted as all pattern.\n2097 | \n2098 |         return self._rewrite(pattern, rule, method, **hints)\n```\n"}, {"content": "Let me also check the `sign()` implementation since it's mentioned in the issue:\n\n<function=search_code_snippets>\n<parameter=search_terms>['def sign', '_eval_rewrite_as_abs']</parameter>\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "toolu_01", "name": "search_code_snippets", "content": "OBSERVATION:\n##Searching for ter