self.n_samples_seen_ = 0\n206 |         self.mean_ = 0.0\n207 |         self.var_ = 0.0\n208 |         self.singular_values_ = None\n209 |         self.explained_variance_ = None\n210 |         self.explained_variance_ratio_ = None\n211 |         self.noise_variance_ = None\n212 | \n213 |         X = self._validate_data(\n214 |             X,\n215 |             accept_sparse=[\"csr\", \"csc\", \"lil\"],\n216 |             copy=self.copy,\n217 |             dtype=[np.float64, np.float32],\n218 |         )\n219 |         n_samples, n_features = X.shape\n220 | \n221 |         if self.batch_size is None:\n222 |             self.batch_size_ = 5 * n_features\n223 |         else:\n224 |             self.batch_size_ = self.batch_size\n225 | \n226 |         for batch in gen_batches(\n227 |             n_samples, self.batch_size_, min_batch_size=self.n_components or 0\n228 |         ):\n229 |             X_batch = X[batch]\n230 |             if sparse.issparse(X_batch):\n231 |                 X_batch = X_batch.toarray()\n232 |             self.partial_fit(X_batch, check_input=False)\n233 | \n234 |         return self\n```\n\nFound file `sklearn/decomposition/_incremental_pca.py`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\nHint: Search `sklearn/decomposition/_incremental_pca.py` for the full content if needed.\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"incremental_pca\", \"OnlinePCA\", \"OnlineNMF\", \"incremental_pca OnlinePCA OnlineNMF\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound class `sklearn/cross_decomposition/_pls.py:PLSRegression`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\nJust show the structure of this class due to response length limitations:\n```\nclass PLSRegression(_PLS):\n\n    # This implementation provides the same results that 3 PLS packages\n    # provided in the R language (R-project):\n    #     - \"mixOmics\" with function pls(X, Y, mode = \"regression\")\n    #     - \"plspm \" with function plsreg2(X, Y)\n    #     - \"pls\" with function oscores